.TH STTY 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
stty \- set terminal options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stty
.RI [ option ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Stty
sets certain I/O options on the current output terminal.
With no argument, it reports the current settings of the options.
The option strings are selected from the following set:
.TP
.B raw
Disable input line assembly and line editing.
.TP
.B \-raw
Restore input line assembly.
.TP
.B echo, \-echo
Enable or disable echoing of typed characters.
.TP
.B opost, \-opost
Enable or disable treating a carriage return as a newline.
With -opost, CR only returns the column; LF advances the line.
.TP
.B sane
Restore cooked input, echo and output postprocessing.
.PP
Several options can be supplied together, for example:
.PP
.B stty raw \-echo
.SH FILES
/usr/man/STTY  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
reset(1), vidmode(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 on success, 1 if standard output is not a console, 2 for invalid options or too many operands.
.SH BUGS
At most five option words are accepted. Raw mode does not turn off interrupt signalling. Baud rates, parity, erase/kill character settings and saved-state operands are not implemented.
